"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[8991],{9094(e,t,n){e.exports=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-limits-quotas.dd8f5095.webp"},85605(e,t,n){e.exports=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-setting-gen-ai-provider.3f8e59c7.webp"},11542(e,t,n){e.exports=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-setting-magic-ai-connection-methods.403cd617.webp"},28979(e,t,n){e.exports=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-setting-magic-ai-general.d57db246.webp"},37425(e,t,n){n.r(t),n.d(t,{comp:()=>h,data:()=>u});var a=n(20641);const i=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-config-overview.e76d0e7f.webp";var o=n(28979),r=n(11542),s=n(85605);const l=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-admin-features.3f484d59.webp",d=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-content-generation.99ac5c8f.webp",c=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-image-enhancement.6275de96.webp";var g=n(9094);const p=n.p+"assets/img/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-scope-taxonomy.6530d588.webp",m={},h=(0,n(66262).A)(m,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="magic-ai-admin-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#magic-ai-admin-configuration"><span>Magic AI Admin Configuration</span></a></h1><p>The administrative configuration center of <strong>Magic AI</strong> is located in your WordPress Dashboard under <strong>Marketplace &gt;&gt; Magic AI</strong>.</p><p>The settings screen is organized into specialized configuration panels accessed through a vertical navigation sidebar:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Admin Tab</th><th>Tab Purpose &amp; Configuration Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>General</strong></td><td>Master marketplace activation toggle for the Magic AI engine.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Providers</strong></td><td>AI provider connections, API keys, Ollama endpoint, and connector status.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Admin Features</strong></td><td>Store manager tools (WYSIWYG text generation, product image creator, AI assistant).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Marketplace Features</strong></td><td>Vendor permissions, text/vision models, usage quotas, inline buttons, and taxonomy scope.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This modular architecture allows store owners to configure store-level authoring tools independently from the permissions, limits, and field boundaries granted to marketplace vendors.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-config-overview.webp"><img src="'+i+'" alt="Magic AI Admin Configuration Center Overview"></a></p><hr><h2 id="general-master-switch" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#general-master-switch"><span>General (Master Switch)</span></a></h2><p>The <strong>General</strong> tab handles global activation and provides a baseline status check for the Magic AI module.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Setting Label</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Functional Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Enabled</strong></td><td>Toggle Switch</td><td>Disabled</td><td>The universal on/off switch for the entire Magic AI ecosystem across the marketplace.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="practical-operational-notes" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#practical-operational-notes"><span>Practical Operational Notes:</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Instant Global Pause:</strong> Toggling this switch off immediately suspends all outgoing AI requests and hides all AI trigger buttons across the store (both admin-facing and vendor-facing).</li><li><strong>Safe Maintenance:</strong> You can switch this off during site migrations, provider billing updates, or scheduled maintenance without losing any configured API keys, model selections, or vendor usage limits.</li><li><strong>Save Requirement:</strong> Always click <strong>Save Configuration</strong> at the top right to apply any change to this switch.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-setting-magic-ai-general.webp"><img src="'+o+'" alt="Magic AI General Settings Master Switch"></a></p><hr><h2 id="providers-api-keys-connection-hub" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#providers-api-keys-connection-hub"><span>Providers (API Keys &amp; Connection Hub)</span></a></h2><p>The <strong>Providers</strong> tab is where you manage connections between your marketplace and external artificial intelligence networks.</p><h3 id="connection-method-auto-detection" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#connection-method-auto-detection"><span>Connection Method Auto-Detection</span></a></h3><p>Magic AI automatically detects your WordPress environment and displays one of two status notices:</p><ol><li><strong>WordPress AI Connectors Detected (Green Notice):</strong><ul><li>Active on modern WordPress environments (WordPress 7.0+) with core AI Connectors enabled.</li><li>Foundation providers—<strong>OpenAI</strong>, <strong>Anthropic</strong>, and <strong>Google</strong>—automatically pull their credentials directly from <code>WordPress Admin &gt; Settings &gt; Connectors</code>.</li><li>Magic AI displays a <strong>&quot;Connected &amp; configured&quot;</strong> badge beside these providers with a direct <strong>Manage →</strong> link to core settings.</li><li>No duplicate API keys need to be entered inside Magic AI for these three services.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Manual API Key Configuration (Informational Notice):</strong><ul><li>Active on standard WordPress installations.</li><li>Each provider is configured independently using direct API keys entered in the fields below.</li></ul></li></ol><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-setting-magic-ai-connection-methods.webp"><img src="'+r+'" alt="Magic AI Providers Connection Method Auto Detection"></a></p><h3 id="supported-providers-credentials" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#supported-providers-credentials"><span>Supported Providers &amp; Credentials</span></a></h3><table><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Credentials Format</th><th>Best Suited For</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>OpenAI</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>High-quality marketing text, product names, short descriptions.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Anthropic (Claude)</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Long-form descriptions, structured specifications, brand consistency.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Google (Gemini)</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Vision-based generation from product photos, image enhancement, general copy.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Groq</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Ultra-fast inference with minimal waiting times during generation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>xAI (Grok)</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Modern, creative product highlight generation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>DeepSeek</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Budget-friendly text generation and attribute extraction.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mistral AI</strong></td><td>Standard API Key</td><td>Compact, highly capable multilingual listing translations.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Ollama</strong></td><td>Local Server Endpoint URL (e.g. <code>http://localhost:11434</code>)</td><td>Completely private, self-hosted open-source AI models.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-setting-gen-ai-provider.webp"><img src="'+s+'" alt="Magic AI Supported Providers and API Keys Configuration"></a></p><hr><h2 id="admin-features-store-owner-ai-suite" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-features-store-owner-ai-suite"><span>Admin Features (Store Owner AI Suite)</span></a></h2><p>The <strong>Admin Features</strong> tab configures the generative AI tools available to store administrators, editors, and catalog managers when managing products in the WordPress backend.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Admin Feature Section</th><th>Configuration Controls</th><th>Key Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>1. Text Generation</strong></td><td>Toggle Switch &amp; Provider Pill Selection</td><td>Enables AI copy generation inside WYSIWYG editors across the admin panel.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2. Image Generation</strong></td><td>Toggle Switch &amp; Provider Pill Selection</td><td>Enables AI product and category image creation on admin screens.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3. Product Page Assistant</strong></td><td>Toggle Switch</td><td>Activates the <strong>Generate content</strong> modal on WooCommerce Add/Edit product screens.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="settings-breakdown" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#settings-breakdown"><span>Settings Breakdown</span></a></h3><h4 id="_1-text-generation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-text-generation"><span>1. Text Generation</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Enabled (Toggle):</strong> Enables AI text creation inside WYSIWYG editors (such as Product Short Description and Full Description) across the admin panel.</li><li><strong>Providers (Multi-Select Pill Group):</strong> Select which providers are permitted for admin text generation (Anthropic, DeepSeek, Gemini, Groq, Mistral, OpenAI, xAI).</li><li><strong>Smart Fallback Failover:</strong> Magic AI attempts generation using the primary active provider. If that provider is unreachable or encounters a quota error, it automatically falls back to the other selected providers in order.</li></ul><h4 id="_2-image-generation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-image-generation"><span>2. Image Generation</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Enabled (Toggle):</strong> Activates the <strong>Generate Image</strong> button on the WordPress editor toolbar for admin product screens.</li><li><strong>Providers (Multi-Select Pill Group):</strong> Select which visual image generation providers to enable (Gemini, OpenAI, xAI).</li></ul><h4 id="_3-product-page-ai-assistant" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-product-page-ai-assistant"><span>3. Product Page AI Assistant</span></a></h4><ul><li><strong>Enabled (Toggle):</strong> When enabled, an AI Assistant button (<strong>Generate content</strong>) appears near the top of the native WooCommerce Add New Product and Edit Product screens, launching a comprehensive multi-field generation modal.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-admin-features.webp"><img src="'+l+'" alt="Magic AI Admin Features Settings"></a></p><hr><h2 id="marketplace-features-multi-vendor-governance" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#marketplace-features-multi-vendor-governance"><span>Marketplace Features (Multi-Vendor Governance)</span></a></h2><p>The <strong>Marketplace Features</strong> tab defines the rules, approved models, quota limits, and field boundaries for all marketplace vendors.</p><h3 id="section-1-product-content-generation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#section-1-product-content-generation"><span>Section 1: Product Content Generation</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Enable (Master Switch):</strong> Master switch for vendor-facing AI generation. When OFF, no vendor can generate product content, regardless of other settings.</li><li><strong>Model:</strong> The specific language model used for text-only generation (e.g., <code>gpt-4o-mini</code>, <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code>, <code>claude-3-5-haiku</code>).</li><li><strong>Allow Reference Images:</strong> Toggle switch. When enabled, sellers can upload photos of physical items for vision-capable models to inspect and analyze.</li><li><strong>Vision Model:</strong> The multimodal model used when vendors attach photos (e.g., <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code>, <code>gpt-4o</code>).</li><li><strong>Maximum Reference Images:</strong> Number input (1 to 10; default is 3). Restricts how many photos a vendor can attach per generation request.</li><li><strong>Let Sellers Choose Fields:</strong> Toggle switch. When ON, sellers can select which specific fields they want AI to draft. When OFF, all eligible fields are drafted automatically.</li><li><strong>Overwrite Filled Attributes:</strong> Toggle switch. When OFF, AI only drafts into empty fields, protecting text the seller already typed.</li><li><strong>Inline Magic AI Buttons:</strong> Multi-select list. Displays dedicated Magic AI buttons beside specific fields (<code>Product Name</code>, <code>Short Description</code>, <code>Long Description</code>) on the vendor form.</li><li><strong>Create Product with AI:</strong> Toggle switch. Displays the launcher button beside <strong>Add Product</strong> on the seller Products list page.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-content-generation.webp"><img src="'+d+'" alt="Marketplace Product Content Generation Settings"></a></p><h3 id="section-2-image-enhancement" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#section-2-image-enhancement"><span>Section 2: Image Enhancement</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Enable:</strong> Toggle switch. Activates the <strong>Enhance image with AI</strong> button below product thumbnails on vendor forms.</li><li><strong>Image Provider:</strong> Select OpenAI or Gemini for thumbnail enhancement.</li><li><strong>Image Model:</strong> Select the specific visual model (e.g., <code>gpt-image-1</code>, <code>gemini-2.5-flash-image</code>, or Default).</li><li><strong>Image API Key:</strong> Optional dedicated API key used exclusively for image enhancements. Stored encrypted.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-image-enhancement.webp"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Marketplace Image Enhancement Settings"></a></p><h3 id="section-3-limits-quotas" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#section-3-limits-quotas"><span>Section 3: Limits &amp; Quotas</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Per Seller Limit:</strong> Maximum generations allowed per vendor within the chosen timeframe. Leave blank for unlimited generations.</li><li><strong>Limit Period:</strong> Dropdown selector choosing the reset cycle: <strong>Monthly</strong> (default), <strong>Weekly</strong>, <strong>Daily</strong>, or <strong>Lifetime</strong>.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-limits-quotas.webp"><img src="'+g+'" alt="Marketplace Limits and Quotas Settings"></a></p><h3 id="section-4-scope-taxonomy-controls" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#section-4-scope-taxonomy-controls"><span>Section 4: Scope &amp; Taxonomy Controls</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Select Attributes (Allowed Fields):</strong> Restrict which product fields AI can draft (Name, Short Description, Long Description, Prices, Weight, Dimensions, Brand, Tags).</li><li><strong>Suggest Categories:</strong> When ON, AI proposes matching categories from existing store categories.</li><li><strong>Suggest Attributes:</strong> Multi-select list. Limits AI attribute suggestions strictly to existing WooCommerce global attributes (e.g., Color, Size).</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/marketplace-admin-magic-ai-mp-scope-taxonomy.webp"><img src="'+p+'" alt="Marketplace Scope and Taxonomy Settings"></a></p>',50)]))}]]),u=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/magic-ai-admin-settings.html","title":"Magic AI Admin Configuration","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"General (Master Switch)","slug":"general-master-switch","link":"#general-master-switch","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Practical Operational Notes:","slug":"practical-operational-notes","link":"#practical-operational-notes","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Providers (API Keys & Connection Hub)","slug":"providers-api-keys-connection-hub","link":"#providers-api-keys-connection-hub","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Connection Method Auto-Detection","slug":"connection-method-auto-detection","link":"#connection-method-auto-detection","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Supported Providers & Credentials","slug":"supported-providers-credentials","link":"#supported-providers-credentials","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Admin Features (Store Owner AI Suite)","slug":"admin-features-store-owner-ai-suite","link":"#admin-features-store-owner-ai-suite","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Settings Breakdown","slug":"settings-breakdown","link":"#settings-breakdown","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Marketplace Features (Multi-Vendor Governance)","slug":"marketplace-features-multi-vendor-governance","link":"#marketplace-features-multi-vendor-governance","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Section 1: Product Content Generation","slug":"section-1-product-content-generation","link":"#section-1-product-content-generation","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Section 2: Image Enhancement","slug":"section-2-image-enhancement","link":"#section-2-image-enhancement","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Section 3: Limits & Quotas","slug":"section-3-limits-quotas","link":"#section-3-limits-quotas","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Section 4: Scope & Taxonomy Controls","slug":"section-4-scope-taxonomy-controls","link":"#section-4-scope-taxonomy-controls","children":[]}]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/magic-ai-admin-settings.md"}')}}]);